context.linkedIssueBody:
## Summary

The employer-search dropdown in `src/pages/WorkerDashboard.tsx` renders result items as plain `<button>` elements inside an absolutely-positioned `<div>`, but the input and the container have no keyboard accessibility wiring:

```tsx
// src/pages/WorkerDashboard.tsx  (lines 340–364)
{showDropdown && results.length > 0 && (
  <div
    className="absolute z-20 mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-white/[0.1] bg-neutral-900 shadow-xl overflow-hidden"
    // ↑ no role="listbox", no aria-label
  >
    {results.map((emp) => (
      <button
        key={emp.employer_id}
        onClick={() => handleSelect(emp)}
        className="w-full flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-3 ..."
        // ↑ no role="option", no aria-selected, no onKeyDown
      >
        <p className="text-[14px] text-white font-medium">{emp.business_name}</p>
        ...
      </button>
    ))}
  </div>
)}
```

The search input above the dropdown likewise has no `aria-expanded`, `aria-haspopup`, `aria-autocomplete`, or `aria-activedescendant` attributes. A user who cannot use a mouse cannot navigate to, or select, any employer from the list.

## Impact

- **Keyboard-only users** — pressing `↓` after typing does nothing. The only way to pick an employer is clicking with a mouse, locking out keyboard users entirely.
- **Screen-reader users** — no `role="combobox"` / `role="listbox"` / `role="option"` means the dropdown is announced as a generic region; focused items are not read aloud.
- **WCAG 2.1 violation** — Success Criterion 2.1.1 (Keyboard, Level A) requires that all functionality be operable via keyboard. Joining an employer is a core action; failing here affects all keyboard and AT users.

## Proposed Fix

Wire up the [ARIA combobox pattern](https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/combobox/):

```tsx
// src/pages/WorkerDashboard.tsx  — JoinEmployer component

const [activeIndex, setActiveIndex] = useState(-1);
const optionIds = results.map((_, i) => `employer-opt-${i}`);

// On the <input>:
<input
  role="combobox"
  aria-haspopup="listbox"
  aria-expanded={showDropdown}
  aria-autocomplete="list"
  aria-activedescendant={activeIndex >= 0 ? optionIds[activeIndex] : undefined}
  onKeyDown={(e) => {
    if (!showDropdown) return;
    if (e.key === "ArrowDown") {
      e.preventDefault();
      setActiveIndex((i) => Math.min(i + 1, results.length - 1));
    } else if (e.key === "ArrowUp") {
      e.preventDefault();
      setActiveIndex((i) => Math.max(i - 1, 0));
    } else if (e.key === "Enter" && activeIndex >= 0) {
      e.preventDefault();
      handleSelect(results[activeIndex]);
    } else if (e.key === "Escape") {
      setShowDropdown(false);
      setActiveIndex(-1);
    }
  }}
  ...
/>

// On the dropdown container:
<div role="listbox" aria-label="Employer results" ...>
  {results.map((emp, i) => (
    <button
      id={optionIds[i]}
      role="option"
      aria-selected={i === activeIndex}
      key={emp.employer_id}
      onClick={() => handleSelect(emp)}
      ...
    >
      ...
    </button>
  ))}
</div>
```

Reset `activeIndex` to `-1` whenever `results` or `showDropdown` changes.

## Affected File

- `src/pages/WorkerDashboard.tsx` — `JoinEmployer` component, employer search input and results dropdown

